phase4(content-free pivot): strip all per-topic content from prompt system

User principle: "you must not give any content to the research agent! content
means anything that can bias the research towards what you know from memory.
the deep research must have deep research principles and find and organize
and report the workflow on its own!" Reaffirms original session directive
("it must not give any content in the prompt").

This pivot supersedes the v2 redteam audit's commit-2 fixes (registry tier-1
restructure, chronic-case re-tagging, etc.) — the entire registry-content
approach was operating within the WRONG framework. The v1 redteam audit
operated within that wrong framework and so did the recent v2 redteam audit;
both improved registry quality without questioning whether the registry
should pre-fill content at all. User correction: it should not.

Architecture pivot:

REGISTRY (full rewrite to scope-free):
  - DROPPED fields: named_components, expected_cases, topic_priority_sources,
    scope_in, scope_out (all per-topic content)
  - KEPT fields: seq, id, slug, title (4 structural identifiers per topic)
  - Topic boundaries now enforced via SUBSECTION_MAP slot the generator
    builds from all 12 (id, title) pairs

GENERATOR (full rewrite, simpler):
  - DROPPED format functions: _format_named_components, _format_cases,
    _format_sources
  - DROPPED slots: SCOPE_IN, SCOPE_OUT, NAMED_COMPONENTS_BLOCK,
    EXPECTED_CASES_BLOCK, EXPECTED_CASES_MIN, TIER1_SOURCES_BLOCK,
    TIER1_SOURCES_MIN
  - KEPT slots: ID, TITLE, SEQ, slug
  - ADDED slot: SUBSECTION_MAP (12-subsection map with current marked,
    Module 1 / Module 2 split)
  - Pilot-context block emphasizes content-free principle + project-wide
    failure modes only

TEMPLATE (surgical edits):
  - Top intro: added "Content-free by design" paragraph
  - SUBSECTION block: replaced IN-SCOPE/OUT-OF-SCOPE with a methodological
    statement + SUBSECTION MAP + boundary rule + DISCOVERY DIRECTIVE
  - DROPPED: NAMED FRAMEWORK COMPONENTS (TOPIC-BOUND) section
  - DROPPED: EXPECTED HISTORICAL CASE SET (TOPIC-BOUND) section
  - DROPPED: EXPECTED DALIO TIER-1 SOURCE COVERAGE (TOPIC-BOUND) section
  - Cascade Tier 1: emphasized "ALL 7 works MUST be searched and recorded
    in §11 search-trace" — no per-topic subset
  - R17 reframed: "FRAMEWORK-COMPONENT DISCOVERY + COVERAGE" — model MUST
    discover components by primary reading; naming a component from prior
    knowledge without a verbatim citation = rejection
  - R20 reframed: "DALIO CORPUS EXHAUSTIVE SEARCH + SEARCH TRACE" — every
    Tier-1 work must appear as its own §11 search-trace row; no per-topic
    Tier-1 subset
  - R23 reframed: "CASE DISCOVERY + WORKED-EXAMPLE COVERAGE" — model MUST
    discover cases by reading Dalio case panels; no expected-case allowlist;
    §7 covers ALL discovered cases; §11 includes a CASE COMPLETENESS row
  - Schema §7 line: "must cover ALL cases the model discovers"
  - REJECTION TRIGGERS: dropped slot references; added "naming X from prior
    knowledge without verbatim cite = rejection" for R17/R20/R23
  - Slot reference table: simplified to 5 slots (ID, TITLE, SEQ, slug,
    SUBSECTION_MAP)

Regenerated all 12 prompt files. Verification:
  - 0 `<<<` slot leakage in any generated file
  - 0 content tokens (UDEF/BDEL/UINF/four levers/specific cases/etc.) in
    any generated file
  - SUBSECTION MAP renders cleanly with module split + current-marker
  - Cascade Tier 1 source list retained (those are infrastructure: WHERE
    to search, not WHAT to find)
  - R25 book-attribution sanity-check title list retained (disambiguates
    commonly-conflated Dalio works)

Audit findings re-evaluation:
  - C1, M4, C3, M5, m2, M3 — addressed in commit 545899e (still valid)
  - C2, M1, M6, M7, m1, m4, m5 — irrelevant under content-free architecture
    (no per-topic allowlists exist to be contaminated)
  - M2 — irrelevant (per-topic pilot context was per-topic content; now
    project-wide only)
  - C4 — still applies; verification scripts still missing for R17-R25.
    Will address in commit 3.

Files changed:
  - chatgpt_audit_kit/_deepresearch_prompt_registry.py   (760 → 86 lines)
  - chatgpt_audit_kit/_deepresearch_prompt_generator.py  (172 → 173 lines)
  - chatgpt_audit_kit/_deepresearch_prompt_template.md   (~520 → 589 lines)
  - chatgpt_audit_kit/_deepresearch_prompt_*.md (× 12)   (regenerated)

